    "sentence_translations": [
      "Do Chinese People Celebrate Christmas?",
      "",
      "Even though China celebrates the Lunar New Year, which usually occurs around February, ..",
      ".. nowadays some young people like to buy a Christmas tree before Christmas to celebrate Christmas.",
      "",
      "The majority of Chinese people spend Christmas together with their friends or lovers, and like to give each other apples during Christmas.",
      "That is because the \"苹\" in \"apple\" is pronounced the same as \"平\" in \"peace\".",
      "And since Chinese people call December 24th \"peaceful night\", apples given around that time are also known as \"peaceful fruit\".",
      "Giving an apple to a friend on Christmas Eve also means wishing your friend a peaceful New Year.",
      "",
      "Every year, during Christmas, apples become very expensive, especially those apples with Santa Claus or Merry Christmas.",
      "One apple may cost as much as 40 yuan, which is ten times more than a regular apple."
    ]
